.TH DEPLOYWEB 1 "@MAN_DATE@" "deployweb @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
deployweb \- website deployment utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B deployweb
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPROJECT-DIR\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdeployweb\fR is a utility for deploying websites to remote servers. It finds
the project root (by looking for package.json), builds the project using pnpm,
syncs the dist/ directory to the server, and configures Apache virtual hosts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPROFILE\fR
Select server profile name or config file path. If not specified, the first
profile found in ~/.config/deployweb/ will be used.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
Rename the deployment on the server. By default, the basename of PROJECT-DIR
is used.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-domain\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR
Set the domain name for the virtual host. Can include a port in the format
\fIdomain:PORT\fR. Defaults to \fI<name>.com\fR.
.TP
\fB\-p\fR, \fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR
Specify HTTP port(s). Can be specified multiple times. If a port is specified,
only one VirtualHost (HTTP or HTTPS) will be created per port.
.TP
\fB\-\-ssl\fR
Enable HTTPS. Creates HTTPS VirtualHost on the specified port(s), or port 443
if no port is specified.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Reduce verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase verbosity.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display help message and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Display version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Profile configuration files are stored in \fI~/.config/deployweb/\fR. Each profile
is a text file with the following format:
.PP
.RS
.nf
server: <host[:port]>
wwwdir: <path>
user: <ssh username>
identity_file: <keyfile>
visual_host_key: yes/no
sudo_pw: <password>
options: <apache directory options>
.fi
.RE
.PP
The configuration options are:
.TP
\fIserver\fR
Server hostname or IP address, optionally followed by a colon and port number.
.TP
\fIwwwdir\fR
Base directory on the server where websites are deployed.
.TP
\fIuser\fR (optional)
SSH username for connecting to the server.
.TP
\fIidentity_file\fR (optional)
Path to SSH private key file.
.TP
\fIvisual_host_key\fR (optional)
Set to "yes" or "no" to control SSH host key verification
(StrictHostKeyChecking).
.TP
\fIsudo_pw\fR (optional)
Sudo password for remote commands. When specified, uses \fBsudo -A\fR
with an askpass script that reads from \fILC_SUDO_PW\fR environment
variable.
.TP
\fIoptions\fR (optional)
Apache Directory options. Defaults to "\-Indexes +FollowSymLinks" if
not specified.
.SH WORKFLOW
The deployment process follows these steps:
.IP 1. 4
Find project root by searching for package.json starting from PROJECT-DIR
.IP 2. 4
Build the project using \fBpnpm build\fR
.IP 3. 4
Rsync the dist/ directory to the server at \fI<wwwdir>/<name>\fR
.IP 4. 4
Generate and install Apache virtual host configuration
.IP 5. 4
Enable the site and reload Apache
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Deploy to default profile:
.B deployweb /path/to/project
.TP
Deploy with specific profile and domain:
.B deployweb -c production -d example.com /path/to/project
.TP
Deploy with HTTPS on custom port:
.B deployweb -d example.com:8443 --ssl /path/to/project
.TP
Deploy with multiple HTTP ports:
.B deployweb -p 80 -p 8080 -d example.com /path/to/project
.TP
Deploy with custom name:
.B deployweb -n mysite -d mysite.com /path/to/project
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/deployweb/\fR
Directory containing profile configuration files.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pnpm (1),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR apache2 (8)
